sequenceDiagram
    actor Customer
    participant System as Ticket System
    participant Triage as Triage Agent
    participant CRM
    participant Tech as Technical Agent
    participant Bill as Billing Agent
    participant KB as Knowledge Base Agent
    participant Route as Routing Agent
    participant Dest as Destination

    Customer->>System: Submit support ticket
    System->>Triage: New ticket event
    activate Triage

    Triage->>CRM: Look up customer
    CRM-->>Triage: Tier and history

    Note over Triage: Classify urgency and type,<br/>set SLA deadline by tier

    par Parallel analysis
        Triage->>Tech: Analyze (if technical)
        activate Tech
        Tech->>Tech: Check logs, status page, docs
        Tech-->>Route: Technical analysis
        deactivate Tech
    and
        Triage->>Bill: Analyze (if billing)
        activate Bill
        Bill->>Bill: Check invoices, payments, policy
        Bill-->>Route: Billing analysis
        deactivate Bill
    and
        Triage->>KB: Search knowledge base (always)
        activate KB
        KB->>KB: Find similar solved tickets
        KB-->>Route: Matches and confidence
        deactivate KB
    end

    deactivate Triage
    activate Route

    Note over Route: Merge results with tier,<br/>urgency and SLA

    alt High KB confidence, not critical
        Route->>Dest: Auto-response (~40%)
        Dest-->>Customer: Solution from KB
    else Urgent or SLA at risk
        Route->>Dest: Escalate to team lead (~5%)
        Note over Dest: Priority handling<br/>with full context
    else Standard case
        Route->>Dest: Route to human team (~55%)
        Note over Dest: Engineering / Finance / L1<br/>with context summary
    end

    deactivate Route

    Note over Customer,Dest: SLA monitored in the background<br/>by the Escalation Agent (every ~5 min)
